# Phone app

Expo SDK 58, React 19, React Native 0.88, TypeScript `strict`. One screen in `mobile/App.tsx`. Do not add Expo Router or `src/app/`. Logic stays in `mobile/src/` and is covered by `npm test` (`tsx --test src/phone.test.ts`).

- Port behavior from `shared/`. Field names are camelCase (`pulsePeriodMs`, `distanceM`). Packet layout and numeric thresholds must match the Python codec and `CueEngine`.
- `routeBetween` uses Mapbox cycling directions when a token is passed, otherwise the OpenStreetMap bike router. Search uses Nominatim. Do not put tokens, keys, or a User-Agent change into git. Keep `ROUTING_USER_AGENT`.
- The map is `StreetMap` plus `tiles.ts` (OSM tiles in a WebView). UI reads `ScreenState`; it does not choose a turn.
- BLE goes through `HelmetLink` and a `Radio`. Production radio is `react-native-ble-plx` in `radio.ts`. Tests inject a fake radio. Connect only when the advertised name is exactly `SmartHelmet`.
- Expo Go cannot run this app. Add native modules with `npx expo install`. Before using an Expo API, read the SDK 58 page under https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v58.0.0/. Native config belongs in `app.json` plugins, not hand-written `ios/` or `android/` projects.
- Check `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm test` from `mobile/` before finishing.
